  m_Name: 1824
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: 'Anglo-Dutch Treaty and Formal British Control 1824 '
  info: "The Anglo-Dutch Treaty solidifies British control of Singapore, ensuring
    its place in the British colonial empire. The treaty resolves territorial disputes
    between Britain and the Netherlands, giving the Dutch control over Indonesia
    while the British retain Singapore and other territories in the Malay Peninsula.
    Under British rule, Singapore\u2019s population grows rapidly as it becomes a
    center for trade, with thriving communities of Chinese laborers, Indian traders,
    and Malay fishermen."
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 4a4ae438d3b4b47c7996954f2fbb7f3c, type: 3}
